Third-party attributions

Upstream method, lists, and calibration (MIT)
---------------------------------------------
The composite scoring method, the slop word/bigram/trigram lists, the
contrast-pattern logic, and the calibration ranges are derived from the
EQ-Bench slop-score project:

    https://github.com/sam-paech/slop-score
    Commit 289264ab2a0df1358ef81ced3c259610ea709514
    Copyright (c) 2025 Sam Paech, MIT License

The canonical embedded data under slop/data/ is generated from that pinned
revision (see tools/datagen and slop/data/manifest.json). The full upstream
license text is preserved at testdata/upstream/LICENSE.upstream.

Vendored development oracle (MIT / Apache-2.0)
----------------------------------------------
testdata/upstream/js/ contains the pinned upstream JavaScript, used only as
a development-time differential oracle (never shipped in the Go binary).
All files are MIT except js/wordfreq.js, which is Apache-2.0 and is vendored
only because metrics.js imports it; it is never executed by the oracle or
the analyzer. No wordfreq data files are vendored.

Dev-only stage-2 dependency (MIT)
---------------------------------
Running the optional stage-2 delta measurement installs wink-pos-tagger
2.2.2 (MIT, https://github.com/winkjs/wink-pos-tagger) into
testdata/upstream/node_modules/ via `npm ci`. It is a development
dependency only and is not part of the analyzer.
